{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-6830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically by\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-4},\\,\\,\\,y=2{t}^{2},\\,t\\ge 2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-6830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for ${t}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-4}\\,⇒\\,{t}^{2}={x}^{2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${t}^{2}={x}^{2}+4$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny=2({x}^{2}+4)=2{x}^{2}+8\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=2{x}^{2}+8.$\n\nFinally, since $t\\ge 2.$ and $x=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-4},$ we must have $x\\ge 0.$\n\nSo, the complete Cartesian equation is\n\n$$\ny=2{x}^{2}+8,\\,x\\ge 0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-6830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "81a59ad3b806c24baae18706bea12a0206a0971ec73dfc37c8476698dc004e3f"} {"question" "q-6830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-6830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=2{x}^{2}+4,\\,x\\ge 0"] ["math" "y=2{x}^{2}+8,\\,x\\ge 0"] ["math" "y=2{x}^{2}-8,\\,x\\ge 0"] ["math" "y=4{x}^{2}+8,\\,x\\ge 0"] ["math" "y=4{x}^{2}-16,\\,x\\ge 0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-6830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=2{x}^{2}+8,\\,x\\ge 0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-24574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as \n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-24574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=\\frac{x}{4} \\\\ y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using double angle formula for cosine and the Pythagorean identity, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-(1-{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}⁡t-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=\\frac{x}{4}$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{2}$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{2} & =2{(\\frac{x}{4})}^{2}-1 \\\\ \\frac{y}{2} & =2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16})-1 \\\\ \\frac{y}{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-1 \\\\ y & =2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-24574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "81a59ad3b806c24baae18706bea12a0206a0971ec73dfc37c8476698dc004e3f"} {"question" "q-24574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-24574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}"] ["math" "y=2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-1)"] ["math" "y=3(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}-1)"] ["math" "y=3{x}^{2}+8"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-24574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-102680" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-5,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-102680" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=x \\\\ y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-5\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=y+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Pythagorean identity ${sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t=1$, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+(y+5)^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is ${x}^{2}+(y+5)^{2}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-102680" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "81a59ad3b806c24baae18706bea12a0206a0971ec73dfc37c8476698dc004e3f"} {"question" "q-102680" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-102680" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x+5)^{2}+(y+5)^{2}=1"] ["math" "(x-5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+(y+5)^{2}=1"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+(y-5)^{2}=1"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}=1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-102680" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}+(y+5)^{2}=1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-276284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{t-4},\\,\\,\\,y=\\frac{t}{2t+1},\\,t\\ne 4,\\,\\,\\,t\\ne -\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,x\\ne $\n{{field-2}}$,\\,\\,\\,x\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-276284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for $t:$\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{t-4}\\,⇒\\,t=\\frac{4x+1}{x}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=\\frac{4x+1}{x}$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{(\\frac{4x+1}{x})}{(2\\cdot \\frac{4x+1}{x}+1)} \\\\ y & =\\frac{(\\frac{4x+1}{x})}{(\\frac{8x+2}{x}+1)} \\\\ y & =\\frac{(\\frac{4x+1}{x})}{(\\frac{9x+2}{x})} \\\\ y & =\\frac{4x+1}{\\cancel{x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{x}}{9x+2} \\\\ y & =\\frac{4x+1}{9x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=\\frac{4x+1}{9x+2}.$\n\nFinally, since $t\\ne -\\frac{1}{2}$ and $x=\\frac{1}{t-4}$ has range $x\\ne 0,$ we must have \n$x\\ne -\\frac{2}{9},\\text{ }0.$ \n\nTherefore, the complete Cartesian equation is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{4x+1}{9x+2},\\,x\\ne -\\frac{2}{9},\\,\\,\\,x\\ne 0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-276284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "81a59ad3b806c24baae18706bea12a0206a0971ec73dfc37c8476698dc004e3f"} {"question" "q-276284" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-276284" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4x+1}{9x+2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-276284" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-276284" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{2}{9}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-321314" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-321314" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=\\frac{x}{5} \\\\ y=-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=-\\frac{y}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the double-angle formula for cosine and the Pythagorean identity, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-(1-{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}⁡t-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=\\frac{x}{5}$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=-\\frac{y}{6}$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{y}{6} & =2{(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}-1 \\\\ -\\frac{y}{6} & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{25}-1 \\\\ y & =-6(\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{25}-1) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{12{x}^{2}}{25}+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=-\\frac{12{x}^{2}}{25}+6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-321314" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "81a59ad3b806c24baae18706bea12a0206a0971ec73dfc37c8476698dc004e3f"} {"question" "q-321314" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"} {"question" "q-321314" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6-\\frac{12}{25}x^2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004207/state.json" "file_sha256" "65fd05b5dbcbeb5e0520df62f7b7dbf5d1e10c613926a9538f19553c57927a96"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1094 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
